Falsifies `inter_process_communication::verification::a_send_to_an_interrupts_rendezvous_is_refused_and_changes_nothing`.

The defect: `send` forgets the interrupt check and decides as it did before DECISIONS §101's
ruling B. `bind_to_interrupt` still sets the flag and nothing else reads it, so every caller
compiles and every other harness here stays green.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(decided, Send::Refused)`, on any seeded state. On one
with a waiting receiver the send rendezvouses with it, which in the kernel is a driver woken with a
sender's words where it expects its interrupt.

